---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Sunken or Floating? — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 38"
  description="Bekhorot 38: lay Beit Hillel's sela over Beit Shammai's drilled hole, paint which parts of a cup become impure, sweep a lens across a firstborn's eye to find the cataract, and schedule the moist-then-dry fodder trial."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@300;400;700;900&display=swap" />

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    .card { background: #11131b; border: 1px solid #262a3a; border-radius: 1rem; }
    .chip { border: 1px solid #3a3f55; border-radius: 0.6rem; padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8rem; transition: background .15s, border-color .15s; text-align: left; }
    .chip:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #191c28; }
    .chip.ok { background: #13261f; border-color: #6cc3a6; }
    .chip.bad { background: #33191a; border-color: #cc5a48; }
    .chip:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: .92; }
    .stamp { display: inline-block; border: 3px solid currentColor; padding: .15rem .7rem; border-radius: .4rem; transform: rotate(-6deg); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .16em; font-size: .72rem; animation: thunk .25s ease-out; }
    @keyframes thunk { from { transform: rotate(-6deg) scale(1.8); opacity: 0; } to { transform: rotate(-6deg) scale(1); opacity: 1; } }
    .light { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; border: 1px solid #3a3f55; border-radius: 999px; padding: .25rem .7rem; font-size: .72rem; }
    .light i { width: .6rem; height: .6rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #3a3f55; display: inline-block; }
    .light.on i { background: #6cc3a6; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #6cc3a6; }
    .light.off i { background: #cc5a48; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #cc5a48; }
    .zone { cursor: pointer; transition: fill .15s, stroke .15s; }
    .zone:focus-visible { outline: none; stroke: #e0b54a !important; stroke-width: 3; }
    .coin { transition: r .5s ease-out, cy .5s ease-out; }
    .cell { height: 2.4rem; border: 1px solid #3a3f55; font-size: .62rem; transition: background .15s; }
    .cell[data-v="m"] { background: #1f4a33; border-color: #6cc3a6; }
    .cell[data-v="d"] { background: #5a4519; border-color: #e0b54a; }
    .tab { border: 1px solid #3a3f55; border-radius: 999px; padding: .2rem .7rem; font-size: .72rem; }
    .tab[aria-current="true"] { background: #2a2414; border-color: #e0b54a; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .chip, .zone, .coin, .cell { transition: none; }
      .stamp { animation: none; }
    }
    button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible, [tabindex]:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #e0b54a; outline-offset: 2px; }
  </style>

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0a0b10] !text-[#e7e9f0]">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#262a3a] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#161a2a] to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs tracking-[0.22em] !text-[#959bb3]">
        <a href="/daf" class="transition-colors hover:!text-[#e7e9f0]">daf yomi arcade</a>
        <span class="mx-2 opacity-40">·</span>bekhorot 38<span class="mx-2 opacity-40">·</span>2026-10-26
      </p>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 80 44" class="mx-auto mb-3 h-12 w-20" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M4 22 Q40 -6 76 22 Q40 50 4 22 Z" fill="#f1ede2" stroke="#e0b54a" stroke-width="2" />
        <circle cx="40" cy="22" r="12" fill="#6b4a2a" />
        <circle cx="40" cy="22" r="7" fill="#0a0b10" />
        <circle cx="44" cy="18" r="2.4" fill="#f1ede2" opacity=".85" />
      </svg>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl !text-[#f4f5fa]">Sunken or Floating?</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-3 text-3xl font-light !text-[#e0b54a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">מְשׁוּקָּע אוֹ צָף</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]">
        A hole in a skull, a cup touched on the outside, a film over a firstborn’s eye, a lamb on a diet of
        wet grass then hay. The daf measures, paints, peers and waits. Four rounds, straight from the daf.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs !text-[#959bb3]">Score: <span id="score" class="font-bold !text-[#e0b54a]">0</span> / <span id="max">0</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-8">

      <!-- ROUND 1 -->
      <section class="card p-5">
        <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#959bb3]">ROUND 1 · 38A:1–2, 16–20</p>
        <h2 class="frank mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">The coin and the hole</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]">
          A skull that is missing a piece no longer imparts impurity in a tent (Oholot 2:3). How big a piece?
          <b>Beit Shammai</b>: the size of a drilled hole. <b>Beit Hillel</b>: enough that a living person would die, which
          Shmuel puts at <b>a sela coin</b>. But a mishna about windows (Kelim 17:12) says a drilled hole <i>is</i> a sela.
          Then where is the argument? For each voice in the Gemara, size the sela against the hole and lay it down.
          Remember: the bigger the required gap, the stricter the view.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2" id="r1tabs" role="tablist"></div>
        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr]">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 240 180" class="w-full rounded-xl bg-[#0d0f16]" role="img" aria-label="A skull with a drilled hole and a coin to lay over it">
            <path d="M30 150 C20 60 80 20 120 20 C160 20 220 60 210 150 Z" fill="#d9d0bb" stroke="#8d846f" stroke-width="2" />
            <path d="M60 140 C70 120 90 118 100 132 M140 132 C150 118 170 120 180 140" stroke="#8d846f" stroke-width="2" fill="none" />
            <circle id="hole" cx="120" cy="70" r="26" fill="#0a0b10" stroke="#5b5443" stroke-width="2" />
            <text id="holeLbl" x="120" y="112" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#5b5443">Beit Shammai’s hole</text>
            <circle id="coin" class="coin" cx="120" cy="160" r="26" fill="#c9a24a" fill-opacity=".82" stroke="#f0d68a" stroke-width="2" />
            <text id="coinLbl" x="120" y="163" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#3b2c08" font-weight="700">sela</text>
          </svg>
          <div>
            <p id="r1who" class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b54a]"></p>
            <p id="r1claim" class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#e7e9f0]"></p>
            <label class="mt-4 block text-xs !text-[#959bb3]" for="coinSize">Beit Hillel’s sela, relative to the hole</label>
            <input id="coinSize" type="range" min="12" max="40" value="26" class="mt-1 w-full accent-[#e0b54a]" />
            <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] !text-[#959bb3]"><span>smaller</span><span>same</span><span>larger</span></div>
            <button id="layCoin" class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-[#e0b54a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] hover:bg-[#191c28]">Lay the coin</button>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span id="lDispute" class="light !text-[#e7e9f0]"><i></i>A real dispute</span>
              <span id="lEduyot" class="light !text-[#e7e9f0]"><i></i>Beit Shammai the stricter</span>
            </div>
            <p id="r1msg" class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="r1more" class="mt-5 hidden"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ROUND 2 -->
      <section id="r2" class="card hidden p-5">
        <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#959bb3]">ROUND 2 · 38A:3–15</p>
        <h2 class="frank mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">Inside, outside</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]">
          Rav Taḥlifa’s “as certain as the testimony of Ḥizkiyya, father of Ikkesh” sends the Gemara into vessels.
          For each case, the red mark shows where the impurity touched. <b>Tap every part that becomes impure</b>, then check.
          Earthenware is impure only through its interior; vessels purified in a mikveh (wood and the like) are impure
          through any side by Torah law; and the Sages added a rabbinic impurity from impure liquids.
        </p>
        <p id="r2count" class="mt-3 text-xs !text-[#959bb3]"></p>
        <p id="r2case" class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#e7e9f0]"></p>
        <svg id="vessel" viewBox="0 0 400 230" class="mt-3 w-full rounded-xl bg-[#0d0f16]" role="group" aria-label="Vessel parts: tap to mark impure"></svg>
        <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          <button id="r2check" class="rounded-lg border border-[#e0b54a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] hover:bg-[#191c28]">Check</button>
          <button id="r2next" class="hidden rounded-lg border border-[#3a3f55] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e7e9f0] hover:bg-[#191c28]">Next vessel →</button>
          <span id="r2stamp"></span>
        </div>
        <p id="r2msg" class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>
        <div id="r2more" class="mt-5 hidden"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ROUND 3 -->
      <section id="r3" class="card hidden p-5">
        <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#959bb3]">ROUND 3 · 38A:21–38B:9</p>
        <h2 class="frank mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">The examiner’s lens</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]">
          Six firstborns come to the expert. Move the lens (drag, or focus the eye and use the arrow keys) until
          you find what is in the eye, read whether it sits <b>in</b> the eye or <b>floats</b> on it, then rule.
          Remember Yoshiya of Usha’s mnemonic: <span class="frank !text-[#e0b54a]" lang="he">בַּרְקָא</span>, the disease of white patches floating over the eye.
        </p>
        <p id="r3count" class="mt-3 text-xs !text-[#959bb3]"></p>
        <svg id="eye" viewBox="0 0 400 240" tabindex="0" class="mt-2 w-full cursor-crosshair touch-none rounded-xl bg-[#0d0f16]" role="img" aria-label="A firstborn's eye under a magnifying lens. Use arrow keys to move the lens.">
          <defs>
            <filter id="blur"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="5" /></filter>
            <filter id="float"><feDropShadow dx="4" dy="6" stdDeviation="2.5" flood-color="#000" flood-opacity=".75" /></filter>
            <filter id="sink"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="1.6" /></filter>
            <clipPath id="lensClip"><circle id="lensC" cx="90" cy="70" r="50" /></clipPath>
          </defs>
          <g filter="url(#blur)" opacity=".75">
            <path d="M20 120 Q200 -20 380 120 Q200 260 20 120 Z" fill="#e9e3d3" />
            <circle cx="200" cy="120" r="72" fill="#6b4a2a" />
            <circle cx="200" cy="120" r="44" fill="#08080b" />
          </g>
          <g clip-path="url(#lensClip)">
            <path d="M20 120 Q200 -20 380 120 Q200 260 20 120 Z" fill="#f1ede2" />
            <circle cx="200" cy="120" r="72" fill="#7a5532" />
            <circle cx="200" cy="120" r="72" fill="none" stroke="#4a2f17" stroke-width="3" />
            <circle cx="200" cy="120" r="44" fill="#060608" />
            <g id="feature"></g>
          </g>
          <path d="M20 120 Q200 -20 380 120 Q200 260 20 120 Z" fill="none" stroke="#8d846f" stroke-width="3" />
          <circle id="lensRing" cx="90" cy="70" r="50" fill="none" stroke="#e0b54a" stroke-width="3" />
          <line id="lensHandle" x1="125" y1="105" x2="150" y2="130" stroke="#e0b54a" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round" />
        </svg>
        <p id="r3read" class="mt-2 min-h-[1.5rem] text-sm italic !text-[#959bb3]">Sweep the lens across the eye…</p>
        <p id="r3case" class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#e7e9f0]"></p>
        <div id="r3btns" class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"></div>
        <p id="r3msg" class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>
        <button id="r3next" class="mt-2 hidden rounded-lg border border-[#3a3f55] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e7e9f0] hover:bg-[#191c28]">Next firstborn →</button>
        <div id="r3more" class="mt-5 hidden"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ROUND 4 -->
      <section id="r4" class="card hidden p-5">
        <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#959bb3]">ROUND 4 · 38B:10–19</p>
        <h2 class="frank mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">The fodder trial</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]">
          Pale spots and streaming tears count as blemishes only if they are <b>constant</b>. For the tears, the test
          is a cure: feed the animal moist fodder, then dry fodder. If it still weeps, it is permanent.
        </p>
        <div id="r4a" class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4"></div>
        <div id="r4cal" class="mt-6 hidden">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b54a]">The calendar</p>
          <p id="r4calPrompt" class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#e7e9f0]"></p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#959bb3]">Tap a half-month to cycle: empty → <span class="!text-[#6cc3a6]">moist</span> → <span class="!text-[#e0b54a]">dry</span>.</p>
          <div id="cal" class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-8 gap-1"></div>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <button id="calCheck" class="rounded-lg border border-[#e0b54a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] hover:bg-[#191c28]">Check the calendar</button>
            <span id="calTally" class="text-xs !text-[#959bb3]"></span>
          </div>
          <p id="calMsg" class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>
        </div>
        <div id="r4more" class="mt-5 hidden"></div>
      </section>

      <div id="final" class="card hidden p-5 text-center"></div>

      <!-- LEARN -->
      <section class="card p-5">
        <h2 class="frank mb-3 text-lg font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.38a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-lg border border-[#262a3a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] transition-colors hover:bg-[#191c28]">Bekhorot 38a on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.38b" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-lg border border-[#262a3a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] transition-colors hover:bg-[#191c28]">Bekhorot 38b on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Oholot.2.3" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-lg border border-[#262a3a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] transition-colors hover:bg-[#191c28]">The skull: Oholot 2:3 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Kelim.25.6" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-lg border border-[#262a3a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] transition-colors hover:bg-[#191c28]">The cup: Kelim 25:6 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.39a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-lg border border-[#262a3a] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b54a] transition-colors hover:bg-[#191c28]">Continue: Bekhorot 39a ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-2 text-xs !text-[#959bb3]">Top works linked to this daf:</p>
        <ul class="grid gap-1 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2">
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.38a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Rashi (77) ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.38a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Rabbeinu Gershom (49) ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.38a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Steinsaltz (40) ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rash_MiShantz_on_Mishnah_Kelim.25.6" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Rash MiShantz on Kelim 25:6 (12) ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.38a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Tosafot (8) ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishneh_Torah,_Firstlings.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Mishneh Torah, Firstlings 2 ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Bekhorot.6.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Mishnah Bekhorot 6:2–3 ↗</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot.4" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#c3c7d8] transition-colors hover:!text-[#e0b54a]">Eduyot 4: Beit Shammai’s leniencies ↗</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var score = 0, max = 0, done = 0, totalTasks = 0;
      var reduce = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      var NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
      var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };
      function sef(ref) { return '<a class="underline decoration-dotted !text-[#e0b54a] hover:!text-[#f4f5fa]" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.sefaria.org/' + ref.replace(/ /g, '_') + '">' + ref + ' ↗</a>'; }
      function addMax(n) { max += n; $('max').textContent = max; }
      function award(n) { score += (n || 1); $('score').textContent = score; }
      function task() { totalTasks++; }
      function finish() { done++; checkDone(); }
      function show(id) { var e = $(id); e.classList.remove('hidden'); return e; }
      function stamp(ok, yes, no) {
        return ok ? '<span class="stamp !text-[#6cc3a6]">' + yes + '</span>' : '<span class="stamp !text-[#cc5a48]">' + no + '</span>';
      }
      function checkDone() {
        if (totalTasks && done >= totalTasks) {
          var f = $('final'); f.classList.remove('hidden');
          f.innerHTML = '<p class="frank text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">' + score + ' / ' + max + '</p>' +
            '<p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">Cliffhanger (38b:19): Rabbi Yoḥanan, in the name of Rabbi Pineḥas ben Arova, says the animal is fed <b>a fig-bulk</b>. Rava reports a dilemma from the West: a fig-bulk at its first meal each day, or…? ' + sef('Bekhorot 39a') + '</p>';
        }
      }
      function mcq(host, prompt, opts, ref, after) {
        addMax(1); task();
        var box = document.createElement('div'); box.className = 'mt-4';
        box.innerHTML = '<p class="mb-2 text-sm !text-[#e7e9f0]">' + prompt + '</p><div class="flex flex-col gap-2"></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>';
        var list = box.children[1], msg = box.children[2], first = true;
        opts.forEach(function (o) {
          var b = document.createElement('button');
          b.className = 'chip !text-[#e7e9f0]'; b.innerHTML = o.t;
          b.onclick = function () {
            if (o.ok) {
              if (first) award();
              b.classList.add('ok');
              Array.prototype.forEach.call(list.children, function (x) { x.disabled = true; });
              msg.innerHTML = o.why + (ref ? ' ' + sef(ref) : '');
              finish(); if (after) after();
            } else {
              first = false; b.classList.add('bad'); b.disabled = true;
              msg.innerHTML = o.why || 'Not quite. Try again.';
            }
          };
          list.appendChild(b);
        });
        host.appendChild(box);
        return box;
      }
      function chain(host, qs, end) {
        var i = 0;
        (function next() {
          if (i >= qs.length) { if (end) end(); return; }
          var q = qs[i++]; mcq(host, q[0], q[1], q[2], next);
        })();
      }

      // ---------- ROUND 1: the coin and the hole ----------
      // rel: -1 sela smaller than the hole, 0 equal, 1 sela larger. Beit Shammai is stricter when his hole is larger (rel -1).
      var voices = [
        { who: 'Rav Ḥisda’s challenge (37b)', claim: 'Beit Shammai’s drilled hole is the large Temple-chamber drill of the window mishna, and that mishna says it equals a sela of Nero. So Hillel’s sela is…', rel: 0, why: 'Exactly the same size. “You have made Beit Shammai and Beit Hillel one and the same.” Rav Taḥlifa falls silent.', ref: 'Bekhorot 37b:20-21' },
        { who: 'Rav Ḥisda, then Rav Taḥlifa', claim: 'Beit Shammai mean a drilled hole <b>and its obstruction</b>, room for the drill to go in and come out. Rav Taḥlifa: don’t say “perhaps,” say it’s certain. So Hillel’s sela is…', rel: -1, why: 'A touch smaller than Shammai’s hole. Now they disagree, and Beit Shammai require more missing bone before the skull stops being impure: Shammai the stricter, as they should be.', ref: 'Bekhorot 38a:1-2' },
        { who: 'Rav Pappa, read with Rabbi Meir', claim: 'The window mishna’s sela is a <b>large</b> drill. Beit Shammai’s unspecified drill is smaller. Rabbi Meir (Oholot 2:3): it’s the doctors’ <b>small</b> bone drill. So Hillel’s sela is…', rel: 1, why: 'Larger than Shammai’s hole. A real dispute, but now Beit Shammai are lenient: a smaller gap already ends the impurity. And we only list Beit Shammai’s leniencies where Eduyot lists them; elsewhere they are the strict ones.', ref: 'Bekhorot 38a:16-19' },
        { who: 'Rav Pappa, read with the Rabbis', claim: 'The Rabbis of Oholot 2:3: Beit Shammai meant the large drill of the Temple chamber, the one the window mishna sizes as a sela. So Hillel’s sela is…', rel: 0, why: 'The same again. Rav Pappa’s answer works only for Rabbi Meir, and the dispute disappears for the Rabbis.', ref: 'Bekhorot 38a:17-18' },
        { who: 'Rav Naḥman', claim: '<span class="frank" lang="he">סֶלַע נִירוֹנִית שָׁנִינוּ</span>: the window mishna meant the big sela of Nero. An ordinary sela, which is Beit Hillel’s, is smaller than even an ordinary drill. So Hillel’s sela is…', rel: -1, why: 'Smaller than Shammai’s hole, whichever drill you read. Dispute restored, and Beit Shammai are the stricter, even for Rabbi Meir.', ref: 'Bekhorot 38a:20' }
