        { at: [130, 108], sages: true, draw: '<path d="M100 98 C120 102 138 107 154 112" stroke="#14100c" stroke-width="3.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" />', read: 'A <b>black thread</b> running out of the iris into the <b>white</b> of the eye.', blem: [true, false], why: 'Rabbi Meir: a blemish, since <i>tevallul</i> is whatever <span class="frank" lang="he">מְבַלְבֵּל</span>, mixes, through the eye. Rabbi Yosei: not a blemish, “there are no blemishes in the white,” which Rav reads from “their eyes stand forth from <b>fatness</b>” (Ps. 73:7): the white is the eye’s fat, not “his eye.” Our mishna is Rabbi Yosei.', ref: 'Bekhorot 38b:8-9' },
        { at: [200, 120], snail: true, draw: '<path d="M200 120 m0 0 a4 4 0 1 1 4 4 a9 9 0 1 1 -11 -9 a15 15 0 1 1 20 16" stroke="#c9c2ae" stroke-width="3" fill="none" filter="url(#float)" />', read: 'A spiral growth, <b>shaped like a snail</b> (<span class="frank" lang="he">חִלָּזוֹן</span>), over the pupil.', blem: true, why: 'A permanent blemish: one may slaughter on account of it.', ref: 'Bekhorot 38b:5' }
      ];
