          ['The old man then asked his student to permit <i>his own</i> firstborn with that blemish. A Sage can’t rule on his own blemishes. How is this allowed?', [
            { t: 'A Sage may teach his students, and they may rule for him. And per Rav Huna, his ruling counts because he taught it <b>before</b> the case came up.', ok: true, why: 'Rav Huna: a scholar ruling on something that concerns him is heeded if he said it before the incident. Lakonya had been teaching this all along.' },
            { t: 'Because it was a clear blemish anyone could see.', ok: false, why: 'The Gemara’s answer is about when he taught it.' },
